Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Offset: a face whose offset vanishes beside a removed face is closed by the
removed face (mitcad#2433).

A box with its top edges rounded 2 mm, shelled inside with the top open and
Sharp corners (the intersection join) by a wall thicker than the rounding:
the roundings' offsets turn inside out. FindVanishingFaces (patch 0100)
finds such faces and has the offsets of the faces on both sides of them
meet each other instead, but only where there is a kept face on both sides:
across the edge to the removed top it found none (a free edge of the shape
without its caps), kept the roundings, and the thick solid failed at any
thickness ("the offset faces do not close up" in MitCad).

Where that edge bounds a removed face, the removed face is now the face
beyond: ConnexIntAcrossVanished leaves such a pair to ContextIntByInt, which
intersects the offset of the kept face on the other side of the vanishing
faces with the removed face, as at an edge between the two, and gives the
section to both edges. Where that section runs past the removed face's edge
instead of inside it (over the vanishing faces, outside the body: a wall no
thicker than the rounding is wide, or a removed face turning towards the
rounding), it is not taken, and the offset fails as before.

Not covered: a wall no thicker than the rounding (the rounding's offset does
not vanish and never meets the removed face it is tangent to: the edge gets
no image, at any thickness below the radius and at the radius itself), and
the arc join (Rounded), whose ContextIntByArc still passes over vanishing
faces.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 2433.

